{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.ext_of_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.ext_of_eval","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L111-L118","doc":"**Uniqueness of the pentagon potential up to the relation.** Two\nq-dilogarithm data with the *same* argument operations and the *same*\nevaluation map are the same datum (the `five_term` proof is a `Prop`, so it\nis unique). Records that the pentagon pins the potential — the algebraic\nshadow of `prop:q-dilogarithm-exists` (uniqueness of the level-2 primitive). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.satisfies_pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.satisfies_pentagon","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L105-L109","doc":"**Forward corollary**: a q-dilogarithm datum's potential satisfies the Mac\nLane pentagon — the dilogarithm *is* a pentagon solution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.pentagon_iff_isDilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.pentagon_iff_isDilog","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L86-L103","doc":"**The pentagon–dilogarithm equivalence (consolidating proposition).**\nFor fixed argument operations `A`, a potential `f` satisfies the Mac Lane\npentagon (the five-term relation) **iff** it is the evaluation map of a\nq-dilogarithm datum with those arguments.\n\nThis is the precise content of \"QOU axioms → dilogarithm naturally\": the\npentagon coherence does not merely constrain `Li₂^q` — being a solution of\nthe pentagon is *equivalent* to being a q-dilogarithm potential. Sorry-free;\nthe two directions are genuine (forward packages the witness, reverse reads\nthe `five_term` field), not a self-assuming projection. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:dilog-pentagon-is-associator","label":"prop:dilog-pentagon-is-associator","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dilog-pentagon-is-associator.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.five_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.five_term","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.eval","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.args","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.args","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.QDilogData","kind":"structure","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L78-L84","doc":"A **q-dilogarithm datum**: an evaluation potential `eval` satisfying the\nfive-term relation for its argument operations. This is the essential data\nof the content-block `QOU.QDilogarithm` (the `pentagon` field), standalone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.FiveTerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.FiveTerm","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L67-L76","doc":"The **Mac Lane pentagon / five-term relation** on a potential `f : H → H`\nwith argument operations `A`: the additive avatar of the categorical\npentagon, in the dilogarithm cross-ratio form\n`f y + f x = f(xy) + f(x(1−y)/(1−xy)) + f(y(1−x)/(1−xy))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.div","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.compl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.compl","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.mul","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs.mk","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.DilogPentagonAssociator.DilogArgs","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverses/DilogPentagonAssociator.lean#L59-L65","doc":"Argument operations of the pentagon / five-term relation: the monoidal\nproduct `mul`, the complement `compl` (`1 − ·`), and `div`. These are the\ncross-ratio face maps of the pentagon. ","signatureChunk":0}]}